.TH "LEAN" "1" "Oct 2026" "lean" "lean Manual"

.SH NAME
lean-fill - Fill missing keys from schema defaults, same_as, and from: sources


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlean fill [profile] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Apply schema rules to fill in missing values:

.PP
• default       — static default value
  • same_as       — copy from another key
  • from:command  — run a shell command
  • from:file     — read a file
  • from:env      — read a process environment variable

.PP
Existing values are never overwritten.

.PP
Examples:
  lean fill
  lean fill production
  lean fill --dry-run


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Show what would be filled without writing

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for fill

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	Target profile


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlean(1)\fP


